   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "〜の ほう が: the ... is more",
     "texto": [
      "To choose one of two things, put the chosen one with **の ほう が**: **バス の ほう が やすい です** (the bus is cheaper).",
      "To compare with something else, use **より**, as you already know: **でんしゃ より バス の ほう が やすい です** (the bus is cheaper than the train)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "〜ほど 〜ない: not as ... as",
     "texto": [
      "To say that something **is not as** something else: **がっこう ほど とおく ない** (it's not as far as the school).",
      "It's always used with the negative."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "いちばん: the most",
     "texto": [
      "**いちばん** means \"the most\" or \"the very\". It goes before the adjective or verb: **すし が いちばん すき です** (I like sushi the most).",
      "There's no need to say \"of all\"."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "〜すぎる: too much",
     "texto": [
      "It's added to the -ます stem without **ます**: **たべすぎます** (I eat too much); with an -i adjective, drop **い**: **たかすぎます** (too expensive). With -na adjectives, **すぎます** goes after the adjective: **しずかすぎます** (too quiet)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
